// ============================================================
// SKILL: Responsive Swing Detection / Real-Time BOS
// Extracted from the AMDM round-2 fix (BUG-008), 2026-07-22.
// Status: code-reviewed; live re-test pending. NOT a standalone
// indicator -- copy these patterns into an engine.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS: ta.pivothigh(N,N) confirms a swing level N bars
// AFTER it forms. By then price is usually already past it, so
// ta.crossover(close, pivotLevel) almost never fires (BUG-008).
// The responsive form uses the prior N-bar extreme directly --
// fires the bar the breakout closes, no confirmation lag,
// non-repainting (the [1] offset keeps the current bar out of its
// own reference range).
// ============================================================

// §1 — Real-time range breakout (BOS)
// float rangeHi = ta.highest(high, len)[1]
// float rangeLo = ta.lowest(low, len)[1]
// bool bosUp    = close > rangeHi and close[1] <= rangeHi
// bool bosDown  = close < rangeLo and close[1] >= rangeLo
//
// The close[1] term makes it fire ONCE per breakout (first closing
// cross), not every bar price stays beyond the range.

// §2 — Sweep-stop placement (companion pattern, from BUG-005)
// The stop for a sweep/reversal signal references the sweep bar's
// ACTUAL wick extreme, never the level that was swept (that level is
// already pierced by definition -- a stop there sits inside the
// sweep zone and dies on the retest):
//   one-bar sweep signal:  stop beyond low / high  (+ ATR buffer)
//   two-bar sweep+reclaim: stop beyond low[1] / high[1] (+ buffer)

// §3 — When you DO want confirmed pivots (structure mapping, not
// entries): ta.pivothigh/pivotlow are fine for drawing frozen
// structural levels the trade will REFERENCE later -- the lag is
// acceptable there because nothing is being triggered by the cross.
// Rule of thumb: pivots for LEVELS, rolling extremes for TRIGGERS.
